# Copy to .env (development) and, for release builds, to .env.production. Both are git-ignored.
# Use the "anon public" key only, NEVER the service_role key.
#
# Development (.env): the Docya Dev project (Dashboard > Project Settings > API), never the production one;
#   scripts that write or delete data refuse production. Optional Docker copy: http://127.0.0.1:54321,
#   keys from `supabase status`.
# Release builds: your hosted project. Dashboard > Project Settings > API: "Project URL" and the
#   anon / publishable key. See docs/HOSTING.md.
#
# After changing either file, restart Metro with: npx react-native start --reset-cache
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Patient text reminders (Semaphore). These are SERVER-SIDE secrets for the send-reminders Edge Function.
# Do NOT fill them in this file: .env is read by the app's build tool and by the test scripts, and a secret key
# has no business next to the app's settings. Put them in supabase/functions/.env (git-ignored, already created)
# and upload with:
#   supabase secrets set --env-file supabase/functions/.env --project-ref <ref>
# The names, for reference:
#   SEMAPHORE_API_KEY=        the key from your Semaphore dashboard (required to send)
#   SEMAPHORE_SENDER_NAME=    optional; the sender name registered on your Semaphore account
# SMS_LIVE=true is set separately, on purpose, when you are ready to send a real text. See legal/SEMAPHORE.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
